Requirements: 5   with obligations: 5

[task-01] Every bullet under a task file's `## Scope exclusions` heading becomes an
    obligation saying the change does not do the excluded work. That holds when the
    bullet ends with a clause explaining the exclusion, such as "Model calls issued by
    the measurement harness, which is not part of a review run." Today a bullet like
    that sometimes becomes an obligation describing the excluded work as something the
    change must do, and the review then reports it as not addressed.
    -> scope-exclusion-bullets-become-absence-obligations  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Every bullet under a task file's `## Scope exclusions` heading is decomposed into
       an obligation that states the change does not do the excluded work.
    -> scope-exclusion-with-rationale-clause-stays-absence  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       A scope-exclusion bullet that ends with a clause explaining the exclusion, such
       as "Model calls issued by the measurement harness, which is not part of a review
       run.", still yields exactly one obligation stating that the change does not do
       the excluded work, and the explanatory clause does not turn the excluded work
       into work the change must do.

[task-02] An obligation that comes from a scope exclusion requires code evidence only,
    never a test. Within one review, two such obligations whose code evidence is the
    same get the same coverage status.
    -> scope-exclusion-obligations-require-code-evidence-only  [functional/explicit, code_and_tests]
       An obligation that comes from a scope exclusion has its required evidence set to
       code evidence only, and no test is ever required for it.
    -> scope-exclusion-consistent-coverage-status  [invariant/explicit, code_and_tests]
       Within a single review, any two scope-exclusion obligations whose code evidence
       is identical are assigned the same coverage status.

[task-03] A regression case in the decomposition prompt tests covers a scope-exclusion
    bullet that ends with an explanatory clause.
    -> regression-case-scope-exclusion-explanatory-clause  [test_demand/explicit, tests_only]
       A regression case in the decomposition prompt tests covers a scope-exclusion
       bullet that ends with an explanatory clause.
       why tests_only: The requirement asks for a regression test case itself; the test
       is the whole deliverable and no separate source change is demanded.

[exclusion-01] Which evidence obligations from the other sections of a task file
    require.
    -> no-change-to-required-evidence-for-other-sections  [invariant/explicit, code_only, satisfied by absence]
       The change does not alter which evidence obligations from the other sections of a
       task file require.
       why code_only: This scope exclusion names work that was not done, and the absence
       of such changes is confirmed by inspecting the diff, so no test can demonstrate
       it.

[exclusion-02] Which model each stage calls.
    -> no-change-to-stage-model-selection  [invariant/explicit, code_only, satisfied by absence]
       The change does not alter which model each stage calls.
       why code_only: This is a scope exclusion naming work not to be done, so it is
       confirmed by inspecting the diff and no test can show that work was absent.

